+### 2. Steps: script or model (`z-nile/engine/dispatch.luau`, pure)
+| name | kind | lessons | its row's phase | where it runs |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `z-ticket` | model | design | capture | a fresh `capture-zn-<n>` worktree |
+| `z-design` | model | design | prep | `prep-<slug>` |
+| `z-raft` | model | design | prep | `raft-<issue id>` (the rafting worktree `raft-plan` ran in) |
+| `z-run` | model | build | deliver (pending until the merge) | the raft's worktree (`./zn worktree <R>`) |
+| `zz-review --mode design\|raft` | model | design | design-review | its author's worktree (`$ZN_CWD`) |
+| `zz-review --mode code` | model | build | code-review (printed for the author's `./zn commit`) | its author's worktree |
+| `z-ready`, `z-stop`, `zz-stats` | script: `./zn ready <id>`, `./zn stop <id>`, `./zn metrics` | — | — | the main checkout |
+| `raft-plan`, `recombine`, `fold`, `release`, `spend` | script: `./zn raft-plan --apply`, … | — | — | the step's worktree |
+| `zz-rules`, `zz-arch`, `zz-test`, any `<project>-…` skill | not a step: read inside one | | | |
+Any other name is an error ("unknown step"). A script step never resolves a model, so `.models.toml` naming `z-ready` changes nothing (the Problem's "nothing stops an agent from being started for them" is closed by the classification). `dispatch.step`, `scriptArgv`, `lessonsOf`, `phaseOf`.
