 ## Acceptance criteria
 
 ### Checked
-<!-- ACn: statement. Each maps 1:1 to a `check "ACn: ..."` line in check.sh. Deterministic. -->
+- AC1: `.models.toml` stacks from the repository root down to the work, a closer file replacing only the keys it sets; a raft takes, per CLI, the stronger of its members' specs whole (higher rank, then larger `max_tokens`) in its own order; only `claude`, `grok` and `agent` and their two runtimes each exist; nothing defaults; and a `zz-review` spec is Opus through `claude` or `agent` and `grok-4.7-xhigh` through `grok`.
+- AC2: every z-nile skill is a model step, a script step or read inside one (ready, stop, recombine and spend are scripts and take no model); a model step's prompt names its skill's file and lessons command and pastes no skill text; the chain goes capture, design, prep gate, raft-plan, z-raft, raft gate, ready, run, run gate from tracker state, passes a prep or raft gate only when allowed, green and mergeable, never passes the run gate, and stops at questions.md, a failed step, an unharvested finding after a review step and a step that moved nothing.
+- AC3: each of the six runtimes starts its CLI headless and unattended with pinned flags, and its stream gives one token count (input + cache writes + output) and a quota signal.
+- AC4: the agent's `git` refuses a push that would put anything but tracker state on `main` (and `--all`, `--mirror`, deleting `main`); its `gh` refuses an unauthorised merge, `--admin` and API writes to merge, protection and ruleset endpoints.
+- AC5: a spend row stores the model id beside its token count (`spend --model`, `commit --model`); a file with no model row keeps nine columns; the model is append-only.
+- AC6: `./zn dispatch` runs a model step in its worktree with the wrapper first on PATH, moves down the order only on quota, kills the step's process group at the cap, on a stall (a wait is quota) and on `stop`, records each attempt's tokens and model, stops the chain at questions.md until `retry`, captures and chains with `new`, and inside a check starts no CLI outside `.cache`.
+- AC7: the skills, the README, AGENTS.md, the usage and the prompt template say what §9 says.
+- AC8: a raft's prompt names its skill files, the architecture map and the lessons command (c0115's and c0120's specs, overridden), and the README spec is green with the dispatcher built.
+- AC9: the real tree's skill links, lessons and audit stay clean, and the root `.models.toml` resolves a model step on all three CLIs.
 
